    <platformActionList>
        <actionListContext>Record</actionListContext>
        <!--
          Arch doc 6.3, and BOTH halves of it are this one list.

          The standard Submit for Approval button is the entry `Submit` /
          StandardButton. Its ABSENCE here is the removal 6.3 requires - the
          platform re-adds it to a record's action bar the moment an approval
          process exists for the object, and this list is the only thing that
          overrides that. An empty <quickActionList/> does NOT suppress it; the
          two lists are unrelated, and Submit has never lived in quickActionList.

          The framework's own action replaces it, under the same label, and
          platformActionList is where an LWC quick action CAN be deployed -
          quickActionList refuses one outright ("You can't add QuickActionType
          LightningWebComponent to a QuickActionList"). This file round-trips:
          retrieve and redeploy both preserve it.

          It is FIRST, at sortOrder 0, so that it renders as a button. The record
          header shows only the first few applicable actions as buttons (three,
          at desktop width) and puts the rest under the overflow menu; last in
          this list, the action was reachable only from there.
        -->
        <platformActionListItems>
            <actionName>Purchase_Request__c.AMF_Submit_For_Approval</actionName>
            <actionType>QuickAction</actionType>
            <sortOrder>0</sortOrder>
        </platformActionListItems>
